elow, the op-amp used is ideal, the transistor has <em>V<sub>BE</sub></em> = 0.7 V and β = 150.<br />\nThe value of output voltage V, of op-amp and nature of feedback present in the circuit will be respectively</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/df685213ba2135594c6048cd2988892f4f9ce852.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Negative feedback, <em>V</em> = 0.7 V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Positive feedback, <em>V</em> = 1.7 V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Negative feedback, <em>V</em> = 1.7 V</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Positive feedback, <em>V</em> = 0.7 V</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/ac361f537554caf151baff361f26bd36973c77b0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>The transfer characteristic of the given precision circuit, will be</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/c49dd6e530f2de6744db43dfdf05c5dc1a3d72dd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/2f46515bcb8f1405e76c37587a154c18eb7140b8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/46449679aae489e0b46f0be0c9ca5485c2de3b91.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/006ded72cdfe2b7e9f22777deecd32ba6d2f2dd3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/403c8f0098db62fb7b11f2a527f60c8f37dcaf32.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/52ef5646ad01ed38a5cabebdf4d851d7834b3101.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Which one of the biasing circuits shows better performance?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Fixed bias</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Collector-to-base</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Self-bias</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nSelf bias is best out of all stability techniques.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the circuit shown below, the value of closed loop gain when <em>R</em><sub>1</sub> = 20 kΩ and <em>R</em><sub>2</sub> = 2 kΩ and <em>A</em> = 10<sup>3</sup> will be ________ .</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/7c1420c5b6358c85f0cc8d782d029c3c7295eb1a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>(Answer upto two decimal places)</div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"1.09","high":"1.09"},"solution":"<p>1.09 (1.05 - 1.15)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/0fd8f6cfb07df890568c02ed14ec5272abad7b40.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the feedback shown in figure below. If <em>h<sub>fe</sub></em> value is very high, then value of feedback factor β assuming transistor is in active region will be ________ m\u0003. (Answer upto two decimal places)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/8f7a5a782284f5fd0757a516541695cf2f6ed2d0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"-0.1","high":"-0.1"},"solution":"<p>-0.10 (-0.1 - -0.09)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/a83b256ead7d63db1253b51ef0ac4b666e89b7d0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Each diode has <em>V</em><sub>γ</sub> = 0.6 V, the diodes <em>D</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>D</em><sub>2</su